# Environment

You are running inside a devc box: a sandboxed container for the project {{.Realm}}/{{.Project}}.

- The project directory is {{.ProjectDir}}. It holds the checkout `main/` and one sibling directory per task worktree; the git directory is `.repo/`.
- You are the user `dev` and cannot become root. If something outside your reach is needed (a system package, network access to another host), say what is needed and ask the user; the user can run commands such as `devc root -- apt-get install -y <package>`.
- Network: {{.NetworkSentence}}
- Git: commits are copied to a relay on the host automatically. Pushing and fetching `origin` is handled by devc, and nothing reaches the upstream repository until the user runs `devc push`. Commit work in progress instead of using `git stash`. Do not run `git gc` or `git worktree prune`.
- Private notes for this project are in {{.Notes}}. They are not part of the repository; never copy them into commits. Long-term memory belongs in {{.Memory}}.
- Tools under /opt/devc are managed from the host. Do not try to update them.
{{- if .Data}}
- Data: the project's data lives in {{.Data.Root}}, shared by all worktrees (each worktree has a `data` symlink to it; it is excluded from git).
{{- if .Data.Inputs}} Inputs ({{join .Data.Inputs ", "}}) are read-only.{{end}}
{{- if .Data.Work}} Put new results in {{join .Data.Work ", "}}.{{end}}
{{- if .Data.Sealed}} In {{join .Data.Sealed ", "}}, create one new directory per run; the user seals a finished run with `devc seal <path>`, after which it can be read but not changed, moved or deleted (not even by you). Never write into a sealed directory; if one must change, ask the user to unseal it.{{end}}
{{- if not .Data.Work}}{{if not .Data.Sealed}} Put new results outside the input directories.{{end}}{{end}}
{{- end}}
